                <h3>More Details</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check" style="color: black;"></i> <span><b>Temperament: </b>A good Stud male should also possess a temperament that is typical and desirable for the breed. This ensures that not just physical but also behavioral traits are passed on to the next generation. It's important to ask and describe what type of cat fits in your breeding program.</span></li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check" style="color: black;"></i><span><b>Breeding Success:</b> Past success in previous litters that are healthy, of good size, and adhere closely to breed standards can also be a factor in a cat's desirability as a stud.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check" style="color: black;"></i><span>As you can see, a Stud male should be in the best condition if you want to add him to your breeding program. ​It's important that you ask the owner if they can show you what kind of checks they have done with their Stud.</span></li>

